# Testing Strategy

## Slice Selection
| Slice | Annotation | Loads | Use For |
|---|---|---|---|
| Controller | `@WebMvcTest(XxxController.class)` | Web layer only | HTTP mapping, validation, serialization |
| Service | none (plain JUnit + Mockito) | Nothing | Business logic |
| Repository | `@DataJpaTest` + `@Testcontainers` | JPA + Postgres | Queries, custom finders, constraints |
| Full | `@SpringBootTest` | Everything | Cross-layer integration, rare |

## Test Naming
`methodName_whenCondition_thenExpectedOutcome`. Examples from this repo:
- `list_whenServiceReturnsPosts_thenReturns200WithBody`
- `create_whenBlankFields_thenReturns400`
- `get_whenMissing_thenReturns404`
- `update_whenFound_thenReturns200WithUpdated`

## Controller Tests — `@WebMvcTest` + `@MockBean`
```java
@WebMvcTest(PostController.class)
class PostControllerTest {
    @Autowired MockMvc mvc;
    @Autowired ObjectMapper json;
    @MockBean PostService service;

    @Test
    void create_whenValidRequest_thenReturns201() throws Exception {
        UUID id = UUID.randomUUID();
        when(service.create(any(PostDto.class))).thenReturn(new PostDto(id, "T", "B", "A", Instant.now()));

        mvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
                .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
                .content(json.writeValueAsString(new PostDto(null, "T", "B", "A", null))))
            .andExpect(status().isCreated())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.id").value(id.toString()));
    }
}
```

## Service Tests — Pure Mockito, No Spring
```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class PostServiceTest {
    @Mock PostRepository repo;
    @Mock PostMapper mapper;
    @InjectMocks PostService service;

    @Test
    void get_whenMissing_thenThrowsNotFoundException() {
        UUID id = UUID.randomUUID();
        when(repo.findById(id)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());
        assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.get(id)).isInstanceOf(NotFoundException.class);
    }
}
```

## Repository Tests — `@DataJpaTest` + Testcontainers (Postgres, not H2)
```java
@DataJpaTest
@Testcontainers
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = Replace.NONE)
class JpaPostRepositoryTest {

    @Container
    static PostgreSQLContainer<?> pg = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:16-alpine");

    @DynamicPropertySource
    static void props(DynamicPropertyRegistry r) {
        r.add("spring.datasource.url", pg::getJdbcUrl);
        r.add("spring.datasource.username", pg::getUsername);
        r.add("spring.datasource.password", pg::getPassword);
    }

    @Autowired JpaPostRepository repo;

    @Test
    void save_whenNewPost_thenFindByIdReturnsIt() {
        UUID id = UUID.randomUUID();
        repo.save(new Post(id, "T", "B", "A", Instant.now()));
        assertThat(repo.findById(id)).isPresent();
    }
}
```

`@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = Replace.NONE)` is mandatory — otherwise Spring swaps in H2 and the test lies.

## Reuse Containers
Declare `PostgreSQLContainer` as `static` to start once per class. For repo-wide reuse, use the Testcontainers singleton pattern.

## What NOT to Test
- Getters/setters/constructors on entities
- MapStruct mappers (the generated impl is tested by the controller/service tests that round-trip through it)
- Spring framework internals
